s its PRs, and `just check` rebuilds a dev [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]extension that no longer matches the linked core source.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]2[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sase_core_p0_agent_maintainability.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/sase_core_p0_agent_maintainability.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-164[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-164/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pinned features, just fast, and a true MSRV in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-fast-loop[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-fast-loop: in sase-core, unify dependency features with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cargo-hakari workspace-hack plus a tool-free check.sh features gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](also run in CI). Add `just fast`, and make rust-version true by [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]deleting the incompatible_msrv allows. Measure a ≤5 s no-edit -p scope [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]switch.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core agent guide, provider shims, module map, README[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-agent-guide[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-fast-loop[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-agent-guide: rewrite sase-core AGENTS.md to the target content, add[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md import shims, add `just modules` and fill the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]missing top-level `//!` summaries. Delete the stale sase_core_py binding[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]manifest and cut the README down to current facts.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]repo-open AGENTS.md hint, sase_repo skill, core memory fix[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]instruction-delivery[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]instruction-delivery: sase repo open names an opened repo's AGENTS.md on[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stderr, the sase_repo skill says the same, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rust_core_backend_boundary core memory stops pointing at ../sase-core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and points at docs/rust_backend.md (sase-15w). Also add a short [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cross-repo pointer in docs/rust_backend.md.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Core pin ratchet workflow opens its PR[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]pin-ratchet-bot[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pin-ratchet-bot: make core-pin-ratchet.yml tolerate the apply path's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exit 2 so it reaches the push and PR steps. Behavior-test the step [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]script (sase-15v).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Dev extension rebuilds when linked sase-core source changes[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]extension-freshness[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]extension-freshness: rust-install stamps the source identity (HEAD plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a dirty digest) it built from. validate_test_environment compares it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with the linked checkout and flags a rebuild through a new status bit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and fingerprint bucket, _setup rebuilds on that bit, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stale-extension flake-baseline entry is retired.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Manage